     "If several codes are logged, work battery, charging and CANBus codes first. (p.25)",
     "ECM normal battery range is 10-15 VDC; outside it the ECM faults to protect itself. (p.91)",
     "Clear the alarm and run the unit. (p.91)",
     "If the code does not come back: Intermittent Alarm Test - check bulletins, torque every harness ground (control box, each engine foot, rear of block), run the Battery and Cables Test, confirm every device has current firmware, run at full load and wiggle the sensor, ECM and ground connections; if it cannot be recreated, call Technical Support. (p.121)",
     "Check the battery connections; clean and tighten. (p.91)",
     "Run the Battery and Cables Test, the AC Battery Charger Test and the Stator Battery Charger (Voltage Regulator) Test; repair any failure and retest. (p.91)",
     "DC volts: back-probe Wire 13A at the master power relay (MPR) COM terminal, then at Pin A, to battery negative. Both = continue; only one = replace harness; neither = check the 15A fuse in Wire 13 (good = replace harness; blown = replace; keeps blowing = ECM Harness Fuse Testing). (p.91)",
     "Battery off; unplug the ECM and inspect pins; take all 4 wires off the MPR and inspect terminals. MPR coil, Wire 608 terminal to Wire 13A terminal A: must be 130-165 ohms (else replace MPR). (pp.91-92)",
