     "Stator Battery Charger (VR) Test: check the VR connector and the VR-to-starter-contactor connection. Battery and J6 off; Wire 13 VR connector to SC ring terminal and Wire 0 VR connector to battery negative must each be 5 ohms or less (check the engine-back ground for Wire 0); the two yellow stator wires at the VR connector must read 5 ohms or less (else replace the stator). (p.114)",
     "Reconnect; note battery voltage, run MANUAL 15 s: voltage rises with no faults = charger OK. Same or lower: unplug the VR and read AC volts 696 to 697 while running 15 s - below 70 VAC = replace the engine stator; 70 VAC or more = replace the VR. (Nominal output 10 A at 13.5 V at 3600 RPM.) (p.114)"
