     "If several codes are logged, work battery, charging and CANBus codes first. (p.25)",
     "Battery and Cables Test, Procedure A: inspect cables at both battery posts, the rear engine foot and the starter; clean/tighten any loose or corroded clamp (replace if corrosion will not clean). Red cable from the starter contactor goes to (+), black cable from the frame ground stud to (-). (p.89)",
     "Procedure B: pull and inspect the controller 7.5A fuse (blown: replace it, charge the battery on an external charger and restart the test). Unplug J6 to disable the charger and read battery open-circuit voltage. 12.1 VDC or less, or no crank: Procedure C. 12.2-12.6 VDC or more: reinstall the fuse and J6, go to Procedure D. (p.90)",
     "Procedure C: conductance-test the battery; 75% of rated CCA or less = replace the battery. (Battery spec: 12 V AGM Group BTX30L, 400 CCA minimum.) The onboard charger will not recharge a dead battery. (p.90, p.89, p.17)",
     "Procedure D: feel the starter control relay (SCR) during a run attempt (rule out alarms that block a run, e.g. CANBus). If it clicks, skip to the Wire 13/16 checks. If not: battery off, all SCR wires off; Wire 56 from J4-12 to the SCR and Wire 0 from the SCR to battery negative must each be 5 ohms or less (else harness); SCR coil across the 56/0 pins must be 130-165 ohms (else replace the SCR). (p.90)",
     "Wire 13 at the SCR to the battery positive cable and Wire 16 at the SCR to the starter solenoid must each be 5 ohms or less, else replace the harness. (p.90)",
