    "name": "O2 Sensor",
    "display": "O2 Sensor",
    "meaning": "O2 sensor data valid but below normal operating range; high severe level. (Generac A0004542981 Rev E (dealer manual), p.25, 30, 84, 107, 108, 112, 113, 121). Remote reset: No.",
    "causes": [
     "Throttle binding - mixer assembly (p.112)",
     "Intake gasket or exhaust leak, loose O2 sensor (p.112)",
     "Fuel pressure out of spec (p.112)",
     "Wire 607/804/14C/820G open - harness (pp.112-113)",
     "No 14C power - master power relay (p.113)",
     "O2 sensor out of 0.1-1.2 V, or ECM (p.113)"
    ],
    "steps": [
     "Check GenService for bulletins first; ignore clearable codes set by connecting/disconnecting the battery, pulling/inserting fuses or firmware updates. (p.25)",
     "Sensor reads 0-1 VDC (higher = richer); readings are inaccurate below about 600 F, so a heater circuit warms it. (p.112)",
     "Clear the alarm and run the unit. (p.112)",
     "If the code does not come back: Intermittent Alarm Test - check bulletins, torque every harness ground (control box, each engine foot, rear of block), run the Battery and Cables Test, confirm every device has current firmware, run at full load and wiggle the sensor, ECM and ground connections; if it cannot be recreated, call Technical Support. (p.121)",
     "Remove the air filter and move the throttle by finger - only a slight drag is normal; binding with no obstruction = replace the mixer assembly. (p.112)",
     "Check the intake gaskets for leaks/tears and the exhaust for leaks; make sure the O2 sensor is tight. (p.112)",
     "Run the Fuel Supply and Pressure Test; adjust if out of spec. (p.112)",
     "Unplug the ECM and the O2 sensor and inspect pins; Wire 607 (ECM 2F), 804 (ECM 4J) and 14C ECM-to-sensor must each be 5 ohms or less; unplug the ETMC and check Wire 820G ECM-to-sensor 5 ohms or less (else harness). (pp.112-113, p.84)",
     "Reconnect; Wire 14C at the sensor to battery ground running in MANUAL should show battery voltage. If not: shut down, lift Wire 14C at the MPR and read the MPR terminal - battery voltage = replace harness; none = Master Power Relay Test. (p.113)",
     "Run at least 2 minutes to warm the sensor; Wire 804 at the sensor to battery ground: outside 0.1-1.2 V = replace the O2 sensor; inside = replace the ECM. (p.113)",
     "Master Power Relay Test: check the 15A Wire 13 fuse; back-probe Wire 13A at MPR COM and Pin A to battery negative (only one live = harness). Battery off, ECM unplugged, all 4 MPR wires off: coil 608-to-13A(A) 130-165 ohms (else MPR); energize the coil with 12 VDC and read 13A(COM) to 14C - under 5 ohms = OK, over 5/OL = replace MPR; then ohm 13A, 608 and 14C MPR-to-ECM (14C under 5 ohms = replace ECM). (pp.107-108)"
    ],
    "clear": "Clear the alarm at the controller and run the unit before diagnosing (p.25). Remote reset from FLEET via the GGCAC radio: not allowed - needs a physical reset at the controller (p.30). Alarms that cannot be remotely reset must be resolved before the controller accepts a firmware update (p.25)."
