     "Clear the alarm and run the unit before going to the action step; if unsure what set it, use the Intermittent Alarm Test to recreate it. (p.25, p.121)",
     "AC Output Voltage Test: remove the controller fascia; DMM on AC volts, engine off, clip the leads across the MLCB load terminals (line-to-line) so they cannot shake loose. (p.63)",
     "MLCB OFF with all loads off, controller to MANUAL, MLCB ON, read: about 238-244 VAC = good; outside that = AVR PWM Output Test. (p.63)",
     "AVR PWM Output Test: J7 breakout harness in line (male to controller, female to generator harness), DMM on Hz, red in the Wire 4 WAGO, black in Wire 0A; clear faults, run MANUAL: about 1500-2000 Hz = pass, go to Brushes and Slip Ring Test; 0 Hz = replace the PZ200. (p.63)",
     "Brushes and Slip Ring Test: inspect brush wiring (straight Wire 4 connector on the brush pin nearest the bearing, right-angle Wire 0A behind it) and brush wear; polish dull slip rings with fine non-metallic abrasive (never emery cloth). (p.64)",
     "Unplug J7; each Wire 0A and Wire 4 brush lead to its J7 pin must be 5 ohms or less (else harness); Wire 4 leads to frame ground must read open (any reading = harness); across each brush holder should match rotor spec 4-15 ohms - in spec go to Rotor Assembly Test. (p.64, p.18)",
     "Remove the suspect brush assembly; continuity from the Wire 4 and Wire 0 terminals to the slip-ring side of the brushes: OL = replace the brush assembly; continuity = Rotor Assembly Test. (p.64)",
     "Rotor Assembly Test: brushes off the rings; positive ring (nearest the bearing) to negative ring must be 4-15 ohms (else replace rotor, then Stator Test); positive ring to chassis ground must show no continuity (continuity = replace rotor); then Stator Test. (p.67, p.18)",
     "Stator Test: lift 11/44 off the MLCB and 22/33 off neutral; check windings against Table 3-3 - 11-22 and 33-44 0.00-0.30 ohms, 11-44 at the stator terminal block 0.00-1.0 ohms, excitation 2-6 0.8-1.5 ohms (OL/out of spec = replace stator); studs 11 and 2 to ground must be OL; no reading allowed between windings (2 or 6 vs 11, 22/33, 44) - any reading = replace stator. (pp.69-70, p.18)",
     "Only after a controller replacement: Voltage Calibration in Field Pro (MLCB OFF, meter Wire 11 then Wire 44 to neutral on the generator side of the MLCB while running, enter as A-N / B-N measured voltage). (p.71)"
