     "If several codes are logged, work battery, charging and CANBus codes first. (p.25)",
     "If the ECM was just replaced it ships with no firmware: clear all alarms, leave the unit in OFF, Service mode on 10 s then off, and wait at least 15 minutes for the update. (p.92)",
     "Clear the alarm and run the unit. (p.92)",
     "If the code does not come back: Intermittent Alarm Test - check bulletins, torque every harness ground (control box, each engine foot, rear of block), run the Battery and Cables Test, confirm every device has current firmware, run at full load and wiggle the sensor, ECM and ground connections; if it cannot be recreated, call Technical Support. (p.121)",
     "Verify battery voltage and all fuses; unplug J6, remove the controller 7.5A fuse and the 15A fuse in Wire 13. (p.92)",
