     "Reconnect J3, J6 and both fuses; DC volts Wire 877 at J3 (J3-9; ECM pin 4F) to battery negative: battery voltage = continue; none = check pin J3-9 on the controller with J3 unplugged - no voltage = replace the controller. (p.93, p.84)",
     "Reconnect everything, let the PZ200 reboot, AC volts Wire 743 to 744 at the controller: 0.75-0.95 V = ECM needs programming (Field Pro); 0.4-0.5 V = firmware update in progress, wait and retest; 1.2-1.35 V = replace the PZ200; over 1.35 V = replace the ECM. (p.93)"
