     "The controller confirms transfer by seeing the T1/00 charger input voltage; if it is not seen after the transfer signal, 2738 is set. (p.119, p.50)",
     "Transfer Control Wires Test background: the controller sends 12 VDC out on Wire 194 (J4-3) to the transfer relay / SACM-FCM and grounds Wire 23 (J4-4) to transfer; if Wire 194 drops below 6 VDC the controller shuts the output off and sets a wiring alarm; clearing the alarm restores 12 VDC unless the short/overload is still there. (p.118, p.58)",
     "Verify battery voltage and all fuses. (p.118)",
     "DC volts at the customer connection WAGO block, Wire 194 to Wire 0: under 6 VDC = Testing Wire 194; 11 VDC or more = Testing Wire 23. (p.119)",
     "Testing Wire 194 (194 is dead while a transfer alarm is active - clear it at each step): lift 194 at the SACM/FCM and read it to the Wire 0 terminal. Above 11 VDC: reconnect and read at the SACM/FCM terminal - under 3 VDC = replace the SACM/FCM; above 11 VDC with no transfer = use the transfer switch diagnostic manual. Under 3 VDC: continue. (p.119)",
     "Lift 194 from the transfer-switch side of the WAGO block: above 11 VDC at the block = replace Wire 194 between the block and the SACM/FCM. Under 3 VDC: lift it from the generator side - wire above 11 VDC = replace the WAGO block; under 3 VDC = continue. (p.119)",
     "Battery off, utility AC off, unplug J4 and inspect pins; check Wire 194 from J4 to the WAGO block for a short to ground: short = replace harness; no short = replace the controller. (p.119)",
