  "installNotes": [
   "Clearances: 3 ft (0.91 m) minimum front and ends; 18 in (457 mm) minimum rear; 5 ft (1.52 m) minimum overhead from any structure/overhang; 5 ft (1.52 m) minimum from operable windows, doors, or openings.",
   "Required fuel pressure at the generator's fuel inlet: Natural gas 3.5-7.0 in water column (0.87-1.74 kPa); LP vapor 10-12 in water column (2.49-2.99 kPa).",
   "Mounted on a Generac composite pad or a code-compliant concrete pad; unit must be installed on a level surface.",
   "Battery is field-supplied, not included with the unit; verify polarity, connect positive cable first, disconnect negative first.",
   "Removable service fence panels cannot be placed within 3 ft (0.91 m) of the generator."
  ],
  "tips": [
   "'Response' is Generac's Costco retail badge; mechanically identical to the equivalent-kW Guardian 999 cc unit.",
   "G0072170 (16KW/816 RESPONSE) has NO owner's or install manual anywhere in Generac's catalog for that G-number. It is placed here on the strength of the Response badge and its own wiring diagram (10000017243, 'WD/SD AC HSB EVO2 60HZ 999') plus engine parts manual A0000347484 ('EV GH816 HSB 2019'). Its 816 cc engine is the G-Force 800 Series with hydraulic lifters, so treat the 14/18 kW rows of the Guardian 10-26 kW family as its mechanical reference, NOT the 999 cc spec column here.",
   "Hunting (surging) at idle with no load on 16/20/22 kW Evolution units with the 990/999 engine is within design if it stays 58-62 Hz - more noticeable in heat and humidity, when the throttle sits right at the small/large bore transition. With low-speed exercise on it runs slower and won't hunt during exercise, and in an outage it only runs fast with no load for a few seconds at warm-up and cool-down. Running with the lid open or a side panel off, or a dirty air filter, also makes it hunt. Never drill holes or break baffles out of the air box, and never fit an aftermarket air filter (Generac SIB17-20-AAC Rev A, dealer bulletin).",
   "Hunting outside 58-62 Hz, or hunting under load, needs diagnosis: fuel pin set for the fuel in use (NG/LP); fuel pressure static, cranking and running - no more than 1 in. H2O drop from no load to full load and never above the owner's manual maximum; correct supply pipe size and the flex line as straight as possible; throttle linkage not binding; no kinked internal fuel line from regulator to mixer; Test 12 - stepper motor cycles on start; Test 60 - magnetos and the wire 18 signal to the controller; run on one cylinder at a time and note the difference; check valve lash (Generac SIB17-20-AAC Rev A, dealer bulletin)."
  ],
